---
import MainLayout from "../../../layouts/MainLayout.astro";
import { Image } from "astro:assets";

// Asumo que tienes una imagen para este post, si no, puedes reutilizar la anterior o una nueva
import blogHero from "../../../assets/rocko-legado.jpg";
---

<MainLayout
    title="The 3-Second Rule: Does your website invite people in? | Otterock Blog"
    description="Discover why 53% of users abandon your site if it takes more than 3 seconds to load and how to fix it with Astro."
    image={blogHero.src}
    type="article"
    articleData={{
        publishedTime: "2024-01-15T08:00:00-05:00",
        authorName: "Sergio Bello",
        section: "Web Performance",
        tags: ["SEO", "Performance", "Astro", "Core Web Vitals"],
    }}
>
    <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto py-20 px-6">
        <header class="mb-12 text-center">
                    <a
                        href="/en/blog"
                        class="inline-block mb-8 text-sm text-otter-deep font-bold hover:text-otter-accent transition-colors hover:underline underline-offset-4"
                    >
                        ← Back to Blog
                    </a>

                    <span
                        class="text-slate-600 font-bold tracking-widest uppercase text-xs mb-4 block font-body"
                    >
                        Performance • 4 min read
                    </span>

                    <h1
                        class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-black text-otter-deep mb-6 leading-tight font-display"
                    >
                        The 3-Second Rule: Does your website invite people in or slam the door in their face?
                    </h1>

                    <p class="text-xl text-slate-700 italic font-body mb-8">
                        "In the digital world, slowness is the language of distrust."
                    </p>

                    <div
                        class="rounded-3xl overflow-hidden shadow-xl mb-12 aspect-video bg-otter-deep"
                    >
                        <Image
                            src={blogHero}
                            alt="Speed optimization and web performance"
                            width={800}
                            quality="mid"
                            format="webp"
                            loading="eager"
                            fetchpriority="high"
                            class="w-full h-full object-cover opacity-90"
                        />
                    </div>

                    <!-- GEO Optimization: Key Takeaways (TL;DR) -->
                    <div
                        class="bg-indigo-50 border border-indigo-100 rounded-2xl p-8 text-left mb-12"
                    >
                        <h2
                            class="text-lg font-black text-otter-deep uppercase tracking-wider mb-4 flex items-center gap-2"
                        >
                            <span class="text-2xl">⚡</span> Key Takeaways (TL;DR)
                        </h2>
                        <ul
                            class="space-y-3 text-slate-700 list-disc list-inside font-medium font-body"
                        >
                            <li>
                                The <strong>3-Second Rule</strong> dictates that 53% 
                                of users abandon if loading exceeds this time.
                            </li>
                            <li>
                                Speed is a <strong>critical ranking factor for Google in 2026</strong>.
                            </li>
                            <li>
                                Generic platforms like WordPress often add "dead weight"; 
                                <strong>Astro</strong> eliminates the unnecessary.
                            </li>
                            <li>
                                The first digital impression is speed: a fast website 
                                conveys respect for the client's time.
                            </li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                </header>

                <div
                    class="space-y-8 text-lg text-slate-700 leading-relaxed font-body"
                >
                    <p
                        class="first-letter:text-5xl first-letter:font-bold first-letter:text-otter-deep first-letter:mr-2 first-letter:float-left"
                    >
                        Imagine you decide to treat yourself and go to that luxury 
                        restaurant everyone is talking about. You get to the entrance, 
                        push the door... and it doesn't open. It's stuck. You struggle a 
                        bit, wait, look through the glass, but no one approaches. How 
                        much time would pass before you simply turn around and find another place?
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        In the physical world, you might wait a minute out of politeness. 
                        On the internet, <strong>you only have 3 seconds.</strong>
                    </p>

                    <section>
                        <h2
                            class="text-3xl font-bold text-otter-deep mb-4 font-display mt-12"
                        >
                            The invisible timer of desire
                        </h2>
                        <p class="mb-4">
                            When a potential client clicks your link from Instagram or 
                            Google, a mental timer activates. It's not something they 
                            decide; it's pure instinct.
                        </p>

                        <div
                            class="bg-otter-sand/50 p-6 rounded-2xl border-l-4 border-otter-deep my-6"
                        >
                            <p class="text-slate-800 italic">
                                "The statistics are relentless: if your page takes more 
                                than 3 seconds to load, <strong>53% of users</strong> will 
                                abandon the site before even seeing your first photo."
                            </p>
                        </div>

                        <p>
                            At <strong>Otterock</strong>, we say that speed isn't just 
                            a technical metric; it's the first impression of your service. 
                            If you sell a "Premium" experience but your website is slow, 
                            you are sending a contradictory message to your client: 
                            <em>"My place is amazing, but getting there is a headache"</em>.
                        </p>
                    </section>

                    <section>
                        <h2
                            class="text-3xl font-bold text-otter-deep mb-4 font-display mt-12"
                        >
                            Why does Google hate waiting?
                        </h2>
                        <p class="mb-4">
                            Google has a mission: for the user to find what they're 
                            looking for quickly. If Google sends someone to your website 
                            and that person leaves after 2 seconds because "it won't load", 
                            the search engine scores a negative point for you.
                        </p>
                        <p>
                            For the algorithm, a slow website is a low-quality website. 
                            It doesn't matter if you have the best prices; if you're not 
                            fast, you'll end up on page 10 of the results, where no one ever goes.
                        </p>
                    </section>

                    <section>
                        <h2
                            class="text-3xl font-bold text-otter-deep mb-4 font-display mt-12"
                        >
                            The "Weight" of Generic vs. The Lightness of Craftsmanship
                        </h2>
                        <p class="mb-4">
                            Most current pages (built on WordPress or Wix) are like a 
                            suitcase full of things you don't need. They carry extra code 
                            and heavy plugins that the client's phone has to process before 
                            showing anything.
                        </p>

                        <p
                            class="text-xl font-bold text-otter-deep text-center my-8 font-display bg-white/60 border border-otter-deep/10 p-8 rounded-2xl italic"
                        >
                            "At Otterock, we use next-generation technologies like Astro 
                            to build only what your business needs. Not an ounce of extra code."
                        </p>

                        <div
                            class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-4 text-center text-sm mt-8"
                        >
                            <div
                                class="p-6 bg-white border border-otter-deep/10 rounded-2xl shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-shadow"
                            >
                                <div class="text-3xl mb-2">🍃</div>
                                <p class="text-slate-700">
                                    <strong>No bloat:</strong> Clean code built from scratch 
                                    for your brand.
                                </p>
                            </div>
                            <div
                                class="p-6 bg-white border border-otter-deep/10 rounded-2xl shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-shadow"
                            >
                                <div class="text-3xl mb-2">📱</div>
                                <p class="text-slate-700">
                                    <strong>Mobile First:</strong> Instant loading even 
                                    with weak signals.
                                </p>
                            </div>
                            <div
                                class="p-6 bg-white border border-otter-deep/10 rounded-2xl shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-shadow"
                            >
                                <div class="text-3xl mb-2">💯</div>
                                <p class="text-slate-700">
                                    <strong>Real Metrics:</strong> 100/100 scores on 
                                    Google PageSpeed.
                                </p>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </section>

                    <section>
                        <h2
                            class="text-3xl font-bold text-otter-deep mb-4 font-display mt-12"
                        >
                            Speed is the New Luxury
                        </h2>
                        <p>
                            Today, true luxury is fluidity. A website that loads instantly 
                            conveys trust and professionalism. It tells the client: 
                            <strong>"We value your time"</strong>.
                        </p>
                        <p>
                            Don't test your site yourself (because your browser already 
                            knows it). Use real tools like Google PageSpeed. If the number 
                            is red, you're losing money every time someone clicks.
                        </p>
                    </section>

                    <hr class="border-otter-deep/10 my-12" />

                    <section
                        class="bg-otter-deep text-white p-8 md:p-12 rounded-3xl text-center relative overflow-hidden"
                    >
                        <div
                            class="absolute top-0 right-0 w-32 h-32 bg-white/10 rounded-full -mr-10 -mt-10 blur-2xl"
                        >
                        </div>

                        <h3
                            class="text-2xl font-bold font-display mb-4 relative z-10"
                        >
                            Does your website pass the 3-second rule?
                        </h3>
                        <p
                            class="mb-8 opacity-90 leading-relaxed relative z-10"
                        >
                            Don't let your clients give up before they even meet you. 
                            At <strong>Otterock</strong> we build high-speed formulas 
                            so your technology runs as fast as your dreams.
                            <br /><br />
                            Do you want a free performance audit?
                        </p>

                        <a
                            href="/en/contacto"
                            class="inline-block bg-white text-otter-deep px-8 py-4 rounded-full font-bold hover:bg-otter-accent hover:text-white transition-all hover:-translate-y-1 shadow-lg relative z-10"
                        >
                            Request a Speed Audit 🚀
                        </a>
                    </section>

                    <!-- E-E-A-T: Author Bio -->
                    <footer class="mt-16 pt-12 border-t border-slate-200">
                        <div class="flex items-center gap-6">
                            <div
                                class="w-20 h-20 rounded-full bg-otter-deep flex items-center justify-center text-3xl shrink-0 overflow-hidden"
                            >
                                👨‍💻 <!-- Placeholder for Author Image -->
                            </div>
                            <div>
                                <p
                                    class="text-xs font-bold text-slate-600 uppercase tracking-widest mb-1"
                                >
                                    Written by
                                </p>
                                <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-otter-deep">
                                    Sergio Bello
                                </h3>
                                <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm mt-1 max-w-lg">
                                    Sr. Specialist in Technical SEO and Growth Strategy. 
                                    Passionate about creating websites that are as fast 
                                    as they are human.
                                </p>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </footer>
                </div>
            </article>
</MainLayout>
